Z||000000||Jhonny||11-07-2000||02:35 AM||||<BR>Does the Hypertech chips show the same ECM codes as original GM chips do ?<BR>My ECM has the Hypertech chip installed currently and I was wondering if I need to install the original one to be able to see the codes.<P>/// Jhonny<P>------------------<BR>Jhonny Sokura<BR>Vadstena, Östergötland Sweden<BR>http://www.vadstena.se/turism/engelsk/index.html||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||11-07-2000||09:06 AM||||yes they woill show the same code as your factory uint... but it has WAY more tolerance for things going wrong. Rich/Lean has changed DRASTICLY. and the code 32 (egr rich/lean faulty takes and act of congress to set this off. why do you think somthings wrong with your car? <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mouse.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||maninblack||11-07-2000||09:48 AM||||I have the same chip and so far it runs okay<BR>without setting any codes.<BR>yes, it does have the same code as the factory setting.To max out your chip preformance,I think you should get the bore out t-body and k&n air filter.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jhonny||11-07-2000||11:02 AM||||<BR>The idle is fluctuating up and down so was I interested to see if there was any codes available. <BR>The check engine light never comes on during engine running.<BR>Anyway I will check all vacuum lines for cracks and all other recommended checks found in the archives during next winter. (And the Swedish winter is loong.)<P>/// Jhonny<P>------------------<BR>Jhonny Sokura<BR>Vadstena, Östergötland Sweden<BR>http://www.vadstena.se/turism/engelsk/index.html||||reg||5
Z||000004||88/2.8||11-07-2000||05:30 PM||||Check your egr vacuum sensor, when mine had an erratic idle and the check engine light kept coming on, and when i replaced that it worked fine||||reg||6
Z||000005||Hawk||11-08-2000||05:26 PM||||I live in Cailifornia, does anybody have experience with the hypertech chip passing smog? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||11-08-2000||07:10 PM||||Few chip folks change any closed loop values. Unless they disabled the EGR (NOX will go up), it should be fine. <P>At the same time, the Hypertech (Stage I and II) I looked at didn't change anything when the coolant temperature was above about 3 degrees F and they added a whopping 2 degrees of spark at idle. Get behind me Satan! <P>||||reg||1
